/* lib/store/glyphs.js — THE item glyph library: one filled silhouette per family, and the one rule that
 * maps a registry record (weapon, armor, gear) to its family. Consumed by the store kernel
 * (lib/store/view.jsx: ArtStage, the paper counter and holds) and by the two contextual store bars
 * (player/app.jsx storeGlyph, gm/app.jsx gmStoreGlyph) — one core for the quantity "what does this item
 * look like", so every surface draws the same picture.
 *
 * THE SET (Jason, 2026-09-22, approved on Docs/mockups/store-glyphs-v3.html): 58 icons from game-icons.net
 * chosen by name from candidate sheets, CC BY 3.0, five contributors (Delapouite 33, Lorc 22, Skoll, sbed,
 * Carl Olsen one each). Each entry carries its source path and author; CREDITS rolls the authors up for
 * the footer line the licence asks for: "Icons made by {author}. Available on https://game-icons.net".
 * Provenance rows: Docs/ART_PROVENANCE_LEDGER.md §5. Picks ledger: Docs/mockups/store-glyphs-picks.json.
 *
 * DRAWING: every path is on the library's 512-canvas. `svg(family, size, color)` fits the path's measured
 * bounding box (`bb`, read once in a browser with getBBox) into the requested box and centres it, so a
 * round grenade and a long rifle read as one size — the shared-keyline rule from
 * Docs/mockups/store-glyphs-research/icon-style-rules.md, applied mechanically. Fill only, no stroke; the
 * rarity plate is the host's layer (ArtStage), never baked in.
 *
 * ALIASES keep the eleven family names the first library used (tools, comms, relic, …) rendering, so a
 * caller that still says `glyph('storage')` (the store bars' GEAR tab) gets a picture and not a blank.
 *
 * Classic script (no JSX, no React at load) → window.SWRPGGlyphs. Loaded before lib/store/view.js.
 * Guard: test/store_glyphs.cjs.
 */
